# Optional: pin one instance to a stable UID.
#
# The unit runs with DynamicUser=yes and User=ptokax-%i, so by default each instance
# gets a transient UID that is released on stop. Create a static user of the matching
# name and systemd will use it instead. Do that when file ownership has to survive a
# restart -- restoring a backup tarball, or an external process reading the hub's state.
#
# Install as /usr/lib/sysusers.d/ptokax-<instance>.conf, one file per instance, then:
#   systemd-sysusers
#
# 'u' rather than 'u!' -- the locked-account form needs systemd 257.

u ptokax-main - "PtokaX DC hub (main)" /var/lib/ptokax/main -
